course: dictionary
lesson: 8831
title: Shin: a body part and a climbing word
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Use the context, the words around it, to find out which one the writer means. The word shin is a good example: it names a part of your body, and it is also an action word.
explain: As a noun, your shin is the front of your leg, between your knee and your ankle. «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls with a squeal — he's cut his shin.» Trips, falls and cut tell you the shin is a body part that got hurt.
explain: As a verb, to shin up something means to climb it quickly with your arms and legs. «Shin pads» are a different thing: they protect your shins in sport. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Your shin is the front part of your leg, between your knee and your ankle.
fact: To shin up something means to climb it quickly using your arms and legs.
fact: A knock on the shin hurts a lot because the bone is just under the skin.
fact: In football and hockey, players wear shin pads or shin guards to protect their shins.
fact: Phrases to know: «kick someone in the shin», «shin up a tree», «shin pads».
exercise: «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls, he's cut his shin.» Which part of the body is the shin? | Top of the head | *The front of the leg, between the knee and the ankle | The back of the hand | The inside of the elbow
exercise: Max wants to get the ball out of the tree. What does «shin up the tree» mean? | Sit under the tree to rest | Paint the tree green | Kick the tree hard | *Climb the tree quickly with arms and legs
exercise: «Every sport has rules and safety gear: shin pads in soccer, a helmet and pads in tackle football, and a batting helmet in baseball.» Which gear protects the shins? | Dressing-gown | Sticking-plaster | Batting helmet | *Shin pads
test: Why does a knock on the shin hurt so much? | Shins are the thickest part of the leg | *The bone is just under the skin | It is far away from the brain | The shin has no feeling at all
test: «Badger bathed the Mole's shin with warm water and mended the cut with sticking-plaster.» What did Badger use to mend the cut? | *Sticking-plaster | Slippers | Dressing-gown | Handkerchief
exam: Which sentence uses shin as a verb, meaning to climb? | Shin pads protect the legs in soccer | Kick the ball to Ben | He cut his shin on the step | *Can you shin up the rope in the gym?
